.TH FIX_VIDEO 1 "October 2026" "fix_video 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fix_video \- automated audio dehum, de-crackle, and linear AV sync drift correction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fix_video.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fix_video.sh
is a high-performance shell utility for macOS and Linux designed to repair video and audio recordings corrupted by high-voltage electromagnetic interference (EMI) and asynchronous recording clock drift.
.PP
When filming under high-tension utility transmission lines, two major classes of audio corruption typically occur:
.IP 1. 4
\fBElectromagnetic Interference (Hum, Buzz & Crackle):\fR A fundamental 60 Hz (or 50 Hz) sinusoidal current induces deep audible hum. Additionally, high-voltage corona discharges produce continuous microsecond electrical arcing impulses (crackle) and dense harmonic overtones (120 Hz through 600+ Hz) perceived as an intense frying or buzzing noise. Dual-mic mobile arrays also suffer severe inductive asymmetric corruption on secondary microphones.
.IP 2. 4
\fBClock Misalignment (Linear Sync Drift):\fR Intense EMI can induce timing jitter in internal hardware clock crystals, causing audio and video sampling clocks to record at slightly different rates. Over a multi-minute recording, audio slowly leads or lags behind the video.
.PP
.B fix_video.sh
solves both problems in a single automated pass without generational video loss by passing the video stream through untouched (\fB\-c:v copy\fR) while applying a 7-stage digital signal processing (DSP) filtergraph to the audio track.

.SH DSP PIPELINE
The audio filtergraph is executed in the following strict order:
.TP
.B 0. Channel Selection / Isolation (\fIpan=stereo|c0=c0|c1=c0\fR)
Duplicates the speech-intact primary channel (Left) across both stereo channels, eliminating the EMI-flooded secondary noise-cancelling microphone channel.
.TP
.B 1. Highpass Filter (\fIhighpass=f=90\fR)
Attenuates frequencies below 90 Hz with zero effect on human vocal fundamentals. Eliminates low-frequency electromagnetic mud, handling noise, and wind rumble.
.TP
.B 2. Impulsive Noise Filter (\fIadeclick\fR)
Scans for abrupt non-harmonic waveform discontinuities caused by electrostatic arcing and corona discharges (\fIw=30:o=75:t=2:b=3\fR). Interpolates corrupted samples prior to frequency domain processing.
.TP
.B 3. Spectral Denoiser with Gain Smoothing (\fIafftdn=nr=18:nf=\-45:nt=c:gs=10\fR)
Applies Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) noise reduction with custom noise profiling and gain smoothing to suppress the broadband induction floor without robotic voice flutter.
.TP
.B 4. Harmonic Notch Filters (\fIbandreject\fR)
Applies calibrated Butterworth band-reject filters with Q-factor (\fIQ=15\fR) at the fundamental line frequency and all multiples through the 10th harmonic (60, 120, 180, 240, 300, 360, 420, 480, 540, 600 Hz).
.TP
.B 5. Voice Lowpass Smoothing (\fIlowpass=f=4000\fR)
Rolls off high-frequency electrical sizzle above 4 kHz while retaining full consonant intelligibility.
.TP
.B 6. Downward Expander Gate (\fIagate\fR)
Gently attenuates background induction buzz by 90%+ during pauses between spoken phrases while preserving full voice presence.
.TP
.B 7. Container Sync Alignment (\fIapad / atempo\fR)
Maintains 1.0x natural speech speed and lip-sync, padding trailing silence to match the container video duration.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display summary help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Probe streams, calculate the speed stretch ratio, and print the resulting filtergraph without executing audio re-encoding.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIPATH\fR"
Explicit path for output file. By default, appends \fI_fixed\fR to the input filename in the same directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-channel " <left|right|stereo>"
Select audio channel mapping (default: left).
.TP
.BI \-\-highpass " HZ"
Set the cutoff frequency for sub-rumble highpass filter in Hz (default: 90). Pass 0 to disable.
.TP
.BI \-\-q-factor " Q"
Set the Q-factor for harmonic notch filters (default: 15). Lower values produce wider notches to catch drifting grid harmonics.
.TP
.BI \-\-lowpass " HZ"
Set cutoff frequency for high-frequency sizzle lowpass smoothing (default: 4000). Pass 0 to disable.
.TP
.BI \-\-harmonics " N"
Number of harmonics to notch starting from the base frequency (default: 10, i.e. 60 Hz to 600 Hz).
.TP
.BI \-\-base-freq " HZ"
Fundamental power grid frequency in Hz (default: 60 for North America; set to 50 for European 50 Hz power grids).
.TP
.B \-\-no-declick
Disable stage 2 impulsive de-clicking.
.TP
.B \-\-no-denoise
Disable stage 3 adaptive FFT noise suppression.

.SH ENVIRONMENT & DEPENDENCIES
Requires standard macOS or Linux POSIX environment with:
.TP
.B ffmpeg
Audio/video multiplexing and DSP filtering engine.
.TP
.B ffprobe
Stream header duration extractor.
.TP
.B bc
Arbitrary precision floating point calculator.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Output file written.
.TP
.B 1
Error (missing arguments, missing input file, or missing dependencies).

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Standard automated repair:
.RS
.B ./fix_video.sh /Users/mike/ai/dehum/VID_20261009_111445043.mp4
.RE
.PP
Preview stream ratio and filter chain:
.RS
.B ./fix_video.sh \-\-dry\-run input.mp4
.RE
.PP
Process European 50 Hz recording:
.RS
.B ./fix_video.sh \-\-base\-freq 50 \-\-harmonics 8 input.mp4
.RE

